# REQUIRES: python-api, cuda
# Same-frame forces and energies of `rigid_units = "ON"` (D424;
# #795's validation table, moved to the key; Inputs/rigid_units_frames.py):
# at the input and at later frames of a trajectory of the units, the units
# (mixed) against the general route in double precision within 1.5 times
# the general mixed route's difference, or 1e-5 of the largest force and
# 1e-6 of the potential; the forces projected onto the constraints of the
# waters.
#
# The physical fixture, against an independent f64 all-pairs oracle as
# well: D405's mixture (three waters of TIP3P, two of four sites with a
# linear site, two rigid molecules of three Lennard-Jones atoms, and an
# ion; the two waters taken, the rest anchored), plain cutoffs of 0.9 nm.
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t/mixture
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/kind_pairs_mixture.py %t/mixture
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/rigid_units_frames.py mixture %t/mixture/system.top %t/mixture/system.gro 3 10 --oracle | tee %t/mixture.txt | FileCheck %s -DS=mixture --check-prefixes=CHECK,ORACLE
#
# The same mixture with the site of the waters of four sites listed before
# their frame (D[water-layout]): a copy is read from its first particle,
# and its frame atoms are its places 1 to 3. The oracle takes the site at
# place 3, so the comparison is with the general route alone.
# RUN: mkdir -p %t/site-first
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/kind_pairs_mixture.py %t/site-first site-first
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/rigid_units_frames.py site-first %t/site-first/system.top %t/site-first/system.gro 3 10 | tee %t/site-first.txt | FileCheck %s -DS=site-first
#
# The mixture with an ion listed inside each water of four sites: that kind
# is not of consecutive particles, so ON does not take it and its particles
# run in the rest (D[water-layout]); the run must still agree with the
# general route within the same bounds.
# RUN: mkdir -p %t/scattered
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/kind_pairs_mixture.py %t/scattered scattered
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/rigid_units_frames.py scattered %t/scattered/system.top %t/scattered/system.gro 3 10 | tee %t/scattered.txt | FileCheck %s -DS=scattered
# `mdir run` warns of that kind in its log, as `mdir check` does, and runs
# the other kinds as units.
# RUN: printf '[execution]\ntarget = "GPU"\nprecision = "MIXED"\n[performance]\nrigid_units = "ON"\n' >> %t/scattered/run.toml
# RUN: cd %t/scattered && mdir run run.toml > %t/scattered/run.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SCATTERED-LOG < %t/scattered/run.log
# SCATTERED-LOG: MDIR: rigid units: ON: the units (ON was given)
# SCATTERED-LOG: MDIR: kind 3: not taken: 2 molecules not of consecutive particles; its particles run in the rest
# SCATTERED-LOG: MDIR: warning: kind 3: 2 of 2 molecules are not of consecutive particles in the input
#
# The anchors of the rest, with PME: alanine dipeptide in OPC under NPT
# (Amber's extra point, not linear in its frame, so compared from the first
# step on, where the frame is constrained) and in TIP3P under NVT.
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/rigid_units_frames.py dipeptide-opc %S/Inputs/opc/opc.prmtop %S/Inputs/opc/opc.inpcrd 4 25 --after-input --pme --npt --cutoff=0.8 --pairlist=1.0 --pruned=0.86 | tee %t/dipeptide-opc.txt | FileCheck %s -DS=dipeptide-opc
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/rigid_units_frames.py dipeptide-tip3p %S/Inputs/dipeptide/dipeptide.prmtop %S/Inputs/dipeptide/dipeptide.inpcrd 4 25 --pme --cutoff=0.8 --pairlist=1.0 --pruned=0.86 | tee %t/dipeptide-tip3p.txt | FileCheck %s -DS=dipeptide-tip3p
#
# The triclinic cell: the rhombic dodecahedron of 403 TIP3P waters, whose
# input lies beyond the constrained frame (its radius widened at the
# input), a cutoff of 0.6 nm, from the input on: with plain cutoffs, against
# the oracle as well, and with PME. Its input holds close contacts (a
# Lennard-Jones energy of 12,380 kJ/mol there, 3,145 after 25 steps), where
# the baseline of the other route does not bound the rounding of the
# units' sums (with PME, 1.59 times it at the input): the PME case's bounds
# take the floor of the error model of the sums in f32 as well (--floor;
# Inputs/rigid_units_frames.py, D424, Section 8). The other
# cases keep the baseline alone, which the floor would make looser.
# RUN: sed -e '/^#ifdef/,/^#else/d' -e '/^#endif/d' %S/Inputs/triclinic/water.top > %t/water.top
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/rigid_units_frames.py dodecahedron-cutoff %t/water.top %S/Inputs/triclinic/dodecahedron.gro 3 25 --oracle --cutoff=0.6 --pairlist=0.7 --pruned=0.66 | tee %t/dodecahedron-cutoff.txt | FileCheck %s -DS=dodecahedron-cutoff --check-prefixes=CHECK,ORACLE
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/rigid_units_frames.py dodecahedron %t/water.top %S/Inputs/triclinic/dodecahedron.gro 3 25 --floor --pme --cutoff=0.6 --pairlist=0.7 --pruned=0.66 | tee %t/dodecahedron.txt | FileCheck %s -DS=dodecahedron
#
# CHECK: [[S]]: kinds taken
# ORACLE: frame 0: general double against the oracle
# CHECK: frame {{[01]}} against double: {{.*}} ok
# ORACLE: frame 0 against oracle: {{.*}} ok
# CHECK-NOT: FAILED
# CHECK: [[S]]: rigid units frames passed
